cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the sinew-mocap/solve tree it is a subtree of.
title: sinew-mocap/solve core/spec, the Lean specification of the rotation fitter (vendored)
abstract: >-
  V-Sekai-fire/sinew at 36c926ead40c436b53258f7a897422587f774a17 (the
  archived sinew-mocap/solve), the directory solve/core/spec split with
  git subtree split (5 commits) and added here as a squashed subtree: the
  Lean 4 specification of sinew's solver core, of which this tree uses
  Sinew/Align.lean (rodrigues, ns30, regularize, valid9, jacobi9, kabsch,
  finishAlign, align: a Kabsch-style rotation fit that Rodrigues-solves one
  pair, Newton-Schulz-orthonormalises the covariance of two or more, and
  falls back to a Jacobi-SVD Kabsch solve when valid9 rejects the fast
  path), Sinew/Math.lean (V3, M3, quatToMat) and AlignTest.lean (the
  oracle: a 120-degree rotation recovered at N=1, 2, 5). Anthropometry,
  RigRest, EmitShaders and the SlangCodegen directory come with the split
  and are not built here. Local adaptations: none; this CITATION.cff is the
  only added file. The C port that the drape links is vendor/sinew-align
  (V-Sekai-fire/interactor-gyre), which cites this specification as its
  source. Rotations are row-major 3x3 matrices (AGENTS.md rule 11).
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: K. S. Ernest (iFire)
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/sinew
